{
	"name": "Beastly Aspect",
	"type": "feature",
	"img": "icons/sundries/flags/banner-standard-moon.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p><strong>Passive Effect:</strong> You gain advantage on Perception checks based on Hearing and Smell.</p><p><strong>Active Effect:</strong> <em><strong>Trample</strong></em>. As an action, you may move up to your speed in a straight line, trampling any creatures in your path. Each affected creature must make a Dexterity saving throw against your Maneuver DC, or take 3d10 bludgeoning damage.</p><p>If any of the creatures are reduced to 0 hit points as a result of being Trampled, you may make a melee attack, fueled by the battle’s frenzy. This attack must be within your reach when you end your Trample.</p><p>This action does not reduce your regular movement.</p>",
